  "content": {
    "id": "p23-q48-50-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "48",
    "prompt": "Prove the following identities.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p23-q48-50-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\cot(\\alpha+\\beta)=\\dfrac{\\cot\\alpha\\cot\\beta-1}{\\cot\\alpha+\\cot\\beta}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Identity proved.\n\nTake the reciprocal of the tangent sum expansion and substitute $\\tan\\alpha=\\frac{1}{\\cot\\alpha}$ and $\\tan\\beta=\\frac{1}{\\cot\\beta}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\cot(\\alpha+\\beta)&=\\frac{1}{\\tan(\\alpha+\\beta)}\\\\\\cot(\\alpha+\\beta)&=\\frac{1-\\tan\\alpha\\tan\\beta}{\\tan\\alpha+\\tan\\beta}\\\\\\cot(\\alpha+\\beta)&=\\frac{1-\\frac{1}{\\cot\\alpha\\cot\\beta}}{\\frac{1}{\\cot\\alpha}+\\frac{1}{\\cot\\beta}}\\\\\\cot(\\alpha+\\beta)&=\\frac{\\cot\\alpha\\cot\\beta-1}{\\cot\\alpha+\\cot\\beta}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      },
      {
        "id": "p23-q48-50-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\sec(\\alpha+\\beta)=\\dfrac{\\sec\\alpha\\sec\\beta}{1-\\tan\\alpha\\tan\\beta}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Identity proved.\n\nFactor the cosine sum as $\\cos\\alpha\\cos\\beta(1-\\tan\\alpha\\tan\\beta)$, then take its reciprocal.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\cos(\\alpha+\\beta)&=\\cos\\alpha\\cos\\beta-\\sin\\alpha\\sin\\beta\\\\\\cos(\\alpha+\\beta)&=\\cos\\alpha\\cos\\beta(1-\\tan\\alpha\\tan\\beta).\\end{align*}$$\nTaking reciprocals,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sec(\\alpha+\\beta)&=\\frac{1}{\\cos\\alpha\\cos\\beta(1-\\tan\\alpha\\tan\\beta)}\\\\\\sec(\\alpha+\\beta)&=\\frac{\\sec\\alpha\\sec\\beta}{1-\\tan\\alpha\\tan\\beta}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p23-q48-50-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\operatorname{cosec}(\\alpha+\\beta)=\\dfrac{\\operatorname{cosec}\\alpha\\operatorname{cosec}\\beta}{\\cot\\beta+\\cot\\alpha}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Identity proved.\n\nFactor the sine sum as $\\sin\\alpha\\sin\\beta(\\cot\\beta+\\cot\\alpha)$, then take its reciprocal.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\sin(\\alpha+\\beta)&=\\sin\\alpha\\cos\\beta+\\cos\\alpha\\sin\\beta\\\\\\sin(\\alpha+\\beta)&=\\sin\\alpha\\sin\\beta(\\cot\\beta+\\cot\\alpha).\\end{align*}$$\nTaking reciprocals,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\operatorname{cosec}(\\alpha+\\beta)&=\\frac{1}{\\sin\\alpha\\sin\\beta(\\cot\\beta+\\cot\\alpha)}\\\\\\operatorname{cosec}(\\alpha+\\beta)&=\\frac{\\operatorname{cosec}\\alpha\\operatorname{cosec}\\beta}{\\cot\\beta+\\cot\\alpha}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      }
    ]
  },
